@* IconButton's Overview, written by hand after Button's: labels and variants, sizes and states,
   actions on a row (previewed in each mode) and a tooltip on focus. Accessibility and See also
   come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>An IconButton is a <Anchor Href="docs/components/button">Button</Anchor> with one icon and no visible text, for actions people know by their icon: edit, delete, more. <Code>Label</Code> is required: it's the button's name and its tooltip. When the icon alone isn't clear, use a Button with text.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and variants</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Label</Code> for what the button does, and <Code>Variant</Code>, <Code>Accent</Code> and <Code>Href</Code> as on Button.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="icon-button-variants" />
<TextBlock><Code>Ghost</Code> with a <Code>Neutral</Code> accent suits rows of tools, where a filled button for each would be loud; keep a solid one for the action that matters most.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and states</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Size</Code>, <Code>Loading</Code> and <Code>Disabled</Code> as on Button.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="icon-button-sizes-states" />

<Heading Level="2">Actions on a row</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Href</Code> for a link and <Code>Submit</Code> with <Code>name</Code> and <Code>value</Code> attributes to post which row a button is on, with <Code>OnClick</Code> for the same on interactive pages.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="icon-button-row-actions" />
<TextBlock>IconButton passes <Code>name</Code> and <Code>value</Code> to its button as attributes; unlike Button, it has no <Code>Name</Code>, <Code>Value</Code>, <Code>Form</Code> or <Code>FormAction</Code> parameters. Put the row in the label too ("Delete budget-2026.xlsx"), so screen readers and the tooltip say which one. <Code>OnClick</Code> runs only on interactive pages; on static ones the post is what happens, as with Button.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A tooltip on focus</Heading>
<TextBlock>Wrap it in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/tooltip">Tooltip</Anchor> for a hint that shows on keyboard focus as well as hover, or for more than the label, such as a shortcut.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@WithTooltip</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <IconButton Icon="Lucide.Pencil" Label="Edit" Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost" Accent="Accent.Neutral" />

        @* A link. *@
        <IconButton Icon="Lucide.ExternalLink" Label="Open the docs" Href="https://example.com/docs" />

        @* In a form: posts delete=42 when pressed. *@
        <IconButton Icon="Lucide.Trash" Label="Delete invoice 42" Submit name="delete" value="42"
                    Accent="Accent.Danger" Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost" />
        """;

    private const string WithTooltip = """
        <Tooltip>
            <Content>Bold <Kbd Keys="Ctrl+B" /></Content>
            <ChildContent><IconButton Icon="Lucide.Bold" Label="Bold" Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost" /></ChildContent>
        </Tooltip>
        """;
}
